"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nWe took a bus from Gap Park over to Bondi Beach.  \nAs long as you time the bus right, it's a quick trip.  \nThat said, buses in Australia don't announce the current stop, so you have to keep an eye on Google Maps to know when to get off.\n\nWhen we arrived, lots of people were enjoying a swim.  \nAsian tourists were, as expected, absorbed in taking photos — and so were we.\n\nWe also got to see in person the iconic spot that always comes up when you search for Bondi Beach photos — Bondi Icebergs Pool.  \nIt's a seawater pool built into the rocky cliffs, with an impressive ocean backdrop that makes it Bondi Beach's most famous photo spot.  \nOf course, we took photos there too.\n\nWith a cool breeze blowing and an unobstructed view, it was a great place to just zone out and take it all in.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"